 "notes": "Stretch 2. p.114 row 1 continues LXXXIX line 9 (last numeral on p.113). Numerals: p.114 '10.' at start of row 2 before χeft; '11.' in row 3 between Àusàr and Ani; '12.' in row 5 between Àmentet and maa-f; '1.' before Re of XCI title (row 9, below the rule). p.115: '2.' at start of row 2 before baiu; '3.' in row 3 before the second en (en ba en); '4.' in row 5 before Ḥet Ḥeru; '1.' before Re of XCII title (row 8). Overlines: p.114 row 7 from t'eṭ (3rd group) to the final en; row 8 over śenbet-f and Àusàr only (se not); XCI title: one rule over Re ... χenà-tu, ba and se not overlined, a short separate rule over em, Neter-χert not. p.115 row 1 over t'eṭ àn only; row 5 from àr to pen (end of row); row 6 three rules: àu-f/χeper-f/em, then āper/em, then àn/χenà-tuf (χu and Neter-χert not); row 7 whole row ḥer...nu; XCII row 8 whole row; row 9 from hru through t'eṭ àn (Àusàr, ān, Ani not). Small raised strokes beside ba/χu/ram are coded Z1 (could be the uncoded tick). No footnotes printed on these pages; English on p.115 prints a small raised mark after 'Hathor' with no footnote. 'Q 2' at foot of p.115 is a signature mark, not text. Hieroglyph-line brackets: p.114 row 2 [X1] in erṭāt-[t]en and row 4 [X1] in [te]n; p.115 'k[uà]' brackets are in transliteration only. Ani's det A52 on p.114, A1 (kneeling, arm raised) on p.115."
